      "writtenOn": "2022-01-12T06:22:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I would prefer to let it crash because allocate should always return a non-null value on success (note the NN_TRY will handle any failures reported by IDevice::allocate). This behavior can only be triggered by a faulty canonical implementation, so a caller wouldn\u0027t be able to exploit this.\n\nFWIW, I\u0027ve considered making the Shared* objects (SharedBuffer, SharedDevice, etc.) only constructible with a non-null pointer in the past, which would make this kind of CHECK redundant. As a general question, would you like to see that type of class behavior?",
